# env.optional — paid/external services are optional. The DEFAULT (keyless) path is: the agent
# generates variants + schedule, hands them to the user to deploy/report manually, then scores
# the returned metrics. These keys are used ONLY when the agent AUTO-DEPLOYS the test or
# AUTO-COLLECTS analytics. The gate is never tripped for the core generate-and-score loop.

# --- LinkedIn organic deploy / post-analytics pull ---
# If PHANTOMBUSTER_API_KEY (+ LinkedIn session cookie) or APIFY_API_TOKEN (harvestapi LinkedIn
# actor) is set -> auto-post variants and pull post analytics. If neither is set -> default
# keyless path: the agent returns the posts + schedule for the user to publish, and the user
# pastes back the metrics (manual handoff = the fallback).
PHANTOMBUSTER_API_KEY
APIFY_API_TOKEN

# --- Cold-email A/B sequence create + campaign analytics (pick whichever the agent is wired to) ---
# If LEMLIST_API_KEY or INSTANTLY_API_KEY is set -> auto-create the A/B sequence and pull
# campaign analytics. If not set -> default keyless path: the agent exports the variants +
# even split for the user to run in their own tool and paste the results back.
LEMLIST_API_KEY
INSTANTLY_API_KEY

# --- One-off email sends only (optional convenience) ---
# If SENDGRID_API_KEY or RESEND_API_KEY is set -> send the test emails directly. If not set ->
# default keyless path: hand the email copy to the user to send (manual handoff = the fallback).
SENDGRID_API_KEY
RESEND_API_KEY
